Lock the engine's print-LUT caches, so two threads can render at once

The Android app renders exports on a second engine thread (ExportThread)
while the editor keeps rendering on its own (EngineThread). Everything a
render touches is already safe for that: each render holds only its own
session's lock, the Vulkan backend serialises submits on its dispatch
mutex, the setup cache and the session list are locked, and the error
string is per thread. Two caches are filled lazily without a lock:

  - spk_engine::print_lut_buffers, the device copy of each print LUT and
    the DI view table (lut_buffer_for, di_view_table);
  - PrintLutLibrary::cache_, the host tables (PrintLutLibrary::get).

Two sessions using the same stock for the first time at the same moment
would race on the map insert. This adds one mutex to each and takes it
for the whole lookup-or-fill, so a table is still uploaded exactly once.
print_lut_lock is always taken before the backend's dispatch mutex, never
inside it, so there is no new lock order. Nothing else changes: the
pointers handed out stay valid (std::map and std::unordered_map nodes do
not move), and single-threaded callers pay one uncontended lock per
lookup.

--- a/engine/src/core/print_lut.cpp
+++ b/engine/src/core/print_lut.cpp
@@ -69,6 +69,7 @@
 
 const PrintLut* PrintLutLibrary::get(const Blob& blob, const std::string& stock,
                                      std::string& error) {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> guard(lock_);
     const auto cached = cache_.find(stock);
     if (cached != cache_.end()) return &cached->second;
 
